  "type": "interview",
  "correction_id": "A-COR-0009",
  "rule_id": "A-R-010",
  "note": "Neither can go to 6110 straight away: each fee is $35.00, and any bank fee of $25 or more comes to me (Marv) for review first. Once I've approved it, the bookkeeper books it to 6110. Our policy doesn't say anything about chasing the bounced customer check before approval, and the one without an \"approved\" memo should come to me.",
  "explanation": "The controller (Marv) described existing policy, not a new one. Any First Prairie Bank fee of $25.00 or more needs his approval, and once he approves it the bookkeeper books it to 6110 Bank fees. History fits this: both $35.00 returned item fees were booked to 6110 about 11 days after the bank date, after review. So the recorded outcome of the rule is booking to 6110, not escalating. A-R-010 now books First Prairie Bank fees of $25.00 or more to 6110, after controller approval. It covers all fee types because he said \"any bank fee\". It is not executable because the rule language cannot check for his approval. The investigator must confirm approval before booking. A-R-011 still books fees under $25.00 to 6110 without review. One of the two past fees has no \"approved\" memo. This patch does not settle that item: it needs Marv's review.",
  "patch": {
   "kind": "ops",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "modify",
     "rule_id": "A-R-010",
     "executable": false,
     "text": "A First Prairie Bank returned item fee, service charge, cash handling fee, coin order fee or deposit correction fee of $25.00 or more is booked to 6110 Bank fees by the bookkeeper only after the controller has reviewed and approved it.",
     "when": {
      "item_kind": "bank",
      "direction": "out",
      "description_regex": "RETURNED ITEM FEE|SERVICE CHARGE|CASH HANDLING FEE|COIN ORDER FEE|DEPOSIT CORRECTION FEE",
      "amount_min": 25
     },
     "then": {
      "action": "book",
